<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="description" content="Offline reference for Arm C Language Extensions callables.">
  <title>Overview</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <main class="page">
    <a name="//apple_ref/cpp/Guide/Arm%20C%20Language%20Extensions" class="dashAnchor"></a>
    <header class="hero">
      <div class="eyebrow">Unofficial offline reference</div>
      <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
      <p class="lead">A source-pinned, normalized reference for concrete ACLE callables, their overloads, compilation requirements, semantic mappings, and available performance evidence.</p>
      <dl class="facts">
        <div><dt>Version</dt><dd><code>{{ version }}</code></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Source revision</dt><dd><code>{{ source_revision or "See pinned revisions below" }}</code></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Concrete callables</dt><dd>{{ callable_count }}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Installed runtime dependencies</dt><dd>None; all reference pages and styles are local.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </header>

    <section id="coverage">
      <h2>Coverage</h2>
      {% if family_counts %}
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Family</th><th>Concrete callables</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>{% for family, count in family_counts %}<tr><td>{{ family }}</td><td>{{ count }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      {% else %}<p class="missing-value">No callables were included in this build.</p>{% endif %}

      {% if top_level_guides %}
      <h3>Browse top-level guides</h3>
      <ul class="guide-list">{% for guide in top_level_guides %}<li><a href="{{ guide.href }}">{{ guide.label }}</a><span class="muted"> — {{ guide.count }} callables</span></li>{% endfor %}</ul>
      {% endif %}

      <h3>Maturity</h3>
      <div class="tag-list">
        {% for item in maturity_counts %}<span class="badge maturity maturity-{{ item.key }}">{{ item.label }}: {{ item.count }}</span>{% endfor %}
      </div>
      <p>Release, Beta, Alpha, and Unspecified entries are included. Each callable page shows its own maturity and provenance; inclusion is not a stability guarantee.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="interpretation">
      <h2>How to read this reference</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>One page represents one concrete callable signature. An overloaded alias can resolve to multiple pages.</li>
        <li>Instruction mappings can be semantic, grouped, optional, or optimizer-dependent. A listed mapping does not by itself guarantee emitted machine code.</li>
        <li>Performance data is microarchitecture-specific and appears only with pinned evidence. Values derived from LLVM scheduling models are estimates, not hardware measurements. Missing values are left unresolved rather than invented.</li>
        <li>Compiler flags are examples scoped to the named compiler, version, and base architecture. They are not universal build prescriptions.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="data-quality">
      <h2>Data quality</h2>
      {% if diagnostic_counts %}
      <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Severity</th><th>Diagnostic entries</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for severity, count in diagnostic_counts %}<tr><td>{{ severity | title }}</td><td>{{ count }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
      {% else %}<p>No converter diagnostics are attached to this build.</p>{% endif %}
      <p>Counts include callable-level and catalog-level observations. They count diagnostic entries, not affected callables; multiple diagnostics can apply to one callable.</p>
      <p>Unresolved and partial records remain visibly marked. A page never treats an absent fact as an empty or zero-valued fact.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="source-and-license">
      <h2>Source, attribution, and license</h2>
      <p>This is an unofficial adaptation of the Arm C Language Extensions material. It is not produced, sponsored, or endorsed by Arm. Arm specification prose is adapted under CC BY-SA 4.0 together with the accompanying Arm patent license; CC BY-SA 4.0 is the Adapter's License for this docset's adaptations. Machine-readable ACLE tables used by the converter are distributed under Apache-2.0. LLVM declarations and scheduling-model data retain Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception provenance. GCC is used only for a transient static sampled cross-check and compiler-option references; the generator does not claim to compile samples with GCC, and GCC source and documentation text are not copied into the docset. Each callable page identifies its exact source location, revision, and applicable license.</p>
      <p>The transformation normalizes the source material into a static Dash API-reference layout, expands only source-backed callable forms, joins source-backed fields, and adds search metadata, cross-links, explicit provenance, and diagnostics. These are changes from the upstream presentation. This docset uses an original neutral icon and does not use the Arm corporate logo.</p>
      {% if source_revisions %}
      <h3>Pinned revisions present in this build</h3>
      <ul>{% for revision in source_revisions %}<li><code>{{ revision }}</code></li>{% endfor %}</ul>
      {% endif %}
      <p>Copies of the applicable notices and license terms are included in the docset under <a href="legal/NOTICE.md">Legal notices</a>.</p>
      <p>Arm, Neon, SVE, SME, and related names may be trademarks of Arm Limited (or its subsidiaries). This contribution is not endorsed by Arm.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
